Technical Officials

OCRA Technical Officials can support the fair and consistent delivery of competitive obstacle racing.

Organisers can learn more about the Technical Official pathway and discuss officiating requirements for their event.

Technical Officials:
https://ocra.ie/education/technical-officials


Competition Rules

Competitive events need clear sporting rules.

Current competition information and OCRA rulebooks are available through:

https://ocra.ie/compete/rules


Results

Reliable results are particularly important for:

- Competitive events
- Qualification events
- National Championships
- Rankings
- Historical records

Where an event works formally with OCRA, organisers should discuss result formats and reporting requirements before competition.


Safety Resources

Race organisers should consider appropriate arrangements for:

- Risk assessment
- Obstacle safety
- Medical coverage
- Emergency action planning
- Safety signage
- Course access
- Athlete flow
- Weather
- Incident management


Working With Clubs

OCR clubs can provide an important connection between events and local athletes.

Organisers may be able to work with clubs around:

- Event promotion
- Volunteers
- Athlete participation
- Training
- Community engagement
- Competition development


Growing Competitive OCR

Organisers interested in adding a competitive element to an existing recreational event are encouraged to speak with OCRA.

It may be possible to develop competition gradually rather than immediately attempting to operate a National Championship-level event.

This could begin with:

- Competitive waves
- Consistent categories
- Defined obstacle rules
- Reliable timing
- Trained Technical Officials
- Results publication

and develop further over time.


